1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Delivering the future.

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:09,720
Little robots taking parcels and groceries to the front door due to starting Greenwich, London next year.

3
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:17,340
Up until now, the unpredictable complexity of the real world,

4
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:23,640
infinite variety of hazards and obstacles meant the last mile of delivery needed a human.

5
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:31,440
Not, it seems, any more. Thanks very much.

6
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:40,480
It's us waiting around at home in a five-hour delivery window. We have to take a day off work.

7
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,520
It's so time-consuming and such a waste.

8
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:50,000
Robotics and technology in the current day right now can solve those problems. So that's what we're doing.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,000
There's no doubt that this coming wave of automation, of artificial intelligence and robots like this one,

10
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:05,320
is going to deliver huge advantages to society. It's going to transform our lives, make them more convenient.

11
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:11,800
The question is, is it also going to bring us some problems that society is going to struggle to cope with,

12
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:14,400
not least, more inequality?

13
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:21,960
This is what could happen. With delivery bots, driverless vans, warehouse robots and online retailing,

14
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:29,360
it's possible for a tiny number of people to sew up an entire market that once employed hundreds of thousands or even millions.

15
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:34,360
The few can get fabulously rich. As for the rest,

16
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:40,720
in previous eras of job destruction, when mechanization chased farm workers off the land,

17
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:45,560
it also created new and better-paid jobs in the towns and cities.

18
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:49,720
And when muscle work disappeared, we moved into brain work.

19
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:54,600
But soon, the machines will not only be stronger than us, but smarter too.

20
00:01:56,040 --> 00:02:04,040
Some new jobs will be created. These are robot handlers ready to take control if one of the delivery robots gets into trouble.

21
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:08,880
The real worry is about how many of these new jobs there are going to be.

22
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:17,520
One study estimates that 35% of UK jobs will be automated away in 10 to 20 years' time,

23
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:25,840
and that jobs that pay under £30,000 a year are five times more at risk from automation than jobs that pay above £100,000.

24
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:35,920
Research by McKinsey's has warned that this transformation is happening 10 times faster and at 300 times the scale of the Industrial Revolution.

25
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:42,800
Or, in other words, with 3,000 times the impact of the changes that transform the Victorian world.

26
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:52,480
These sculptures are perhaps a good metaphor for how most politicians have reacted to the challenge until now.

